  "problem": {
    "id": "train-7439",
    "question": "Of 96 oranges, half were ripe. If 1/4 of the ripe oranges were eaten and 1/8 of the unripe oranges were eaten, how many were left eaten in total?",
    "gold": "78",
    "answer": "There were 96/2 = <<96/2=48>>48 ripe oranges.\n48/4 = <<48/4=12>>12 ripe oranges were eaten.\n48/8 = <<48/8=6>>6 unripe oranges were eaten.\nThere were 12+6 = <<12+6=18>>18 oranges eaten in total.\nThere were 96-18 = <<96-18=78>>78 oranges left uneaten.\n#### 78"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many oranges were left eaten in total, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the number of ripe oranges.\n2. Calculate the number of unripe oranges.\n3. Determine how many ripe oranges were eaten.\n4. Determine how many unripe oranges were eaten.\n5. Sum the number of ripe and unripe oranges that were eaten.\n\nStep 1: Calculate the number of ripe oranges.\nThe total number of oranges is 96, and half of them are ripe.\n\\[\n\\text{Number of ripe oranges} = \\frac{96}{2} = 48\n\\]\n\nStep 2: Calculate the number of unripe oranges.\nThe number of unripe oranges is the total number of oranges minus the number of ripe oranges.\n\\[\n\\text{Number of unripe oranges} = 96 - 48 = 48\n\\]\n\nStep 3: Determine how many ripe oranges were eaten.\n\\[\n\\text{Number of ripe oranges eaten} = \\frac{1}{4} \\times 48 = 12\n\\]\n\nStep 4: Determine how many unripe oranges were eaten.\n\\[\n\\text{Number of unripe oranges eaten} = \\frac{1}{8} \\times 48 = 6\n\\]\n\nStep 5: Sum the number of ripe and unripe oranges that were eaten.\n\\[\n\\text{Total number of oranges eaten} = 12 + 6 = 18\n\\]\n\nThus, the total number of oranges that were left eaten is \\(\\boxed{18}\\).",
